# Local-only evidence overlays.
#
# A published bundle carries the standard and the teaching material. The dense pointer
# layer — which file in which private tree witnesses this claim, and which known gaps a
# particular consumer carries against it — is generated by that consumer's mirror into
# `<subject>/.evidence.local.md` and never leaves their machine. A reader without the
# cited codebase cannot use those pointers anyway.
#
# See docs/rkb-profile.md §5. The bundle gate (scripts/check-bundles.mjs) enforces the
# other half of this rule: published frontmatter may not carry evidence keys at all, so a
# leak fails CI rather than shipping quietly.
**/.*.local.md

node_modules/

# Machine identity, and nothing else.
#
# The fleet bridge used to be `.projects.local.json`: slug -> ABSOLUTE path, hidden
# wholesale because the paths were machine-specific. That hid the portable nine tenths
# along with the machine-specific one tenth, and a second machine could not read any of
# it. Redesigned 2026-08-28:
#
#   projects.json          COMMITTED. Slug -> path RELATIVE to a machine root, plus the
#                          machines each project is checked out on. No user names, no
#                          drive letters, nothing machine-specific. Reviewed like any
#                          other registry file.
#   .machine.local.json    IGNORED, below. Three fields, and the only ones that cannot
#                          be shared: which machine this is (Fox, Wolf, ...), the root
#                          the relative paths resolve against, and the contributor id.
#
# `registry.yaml`'s guarantee is unchanged - nothing published here points into a private
# tree, because a relative path names no tree until a machine root is supplied.
#
# Resolved through scripts/lib/projects.mjs; see librarian/projects.md.
**/.*.local.json

# Fleet proposals: the intermediate file a bulk-model pass writes and a reviewer reads.
#
# It is a working artifact, not registry content. What a run DID belongs in the
# librarian vault, in prose, where it is reviewed like everything else here; a large
# machine-written JSON of candidate lines is neither reviewable nor worth a diff. Keep
# the file for as long as the review takes, then let it go.
fleet-*.proposals.json
.worktrees/
